(subclass SoftwareBug InformationRepresentation)

(documentation SoftwareBug EnglishLanguage
  "A SoftwareBug is a defect in a ComputerProgram or in the software
   of a computer system, i.e., a faulty portion of the program's code,
   data, or design. When the program is executed under circumstances
   that trigger the defect, the bug causes the program to produce an
   incorrect or unexpected result, or to behave in ways other than
   those intended by the program's specification or by its users.
   A software bug may exist in a program from its creation or be
   introduced later by modification; it typically remains latent until
   the program is executed with triggering inputs, and it can be
   eliminated by modifying or fixing the program. A single program may
   contain several software bugs.")

(termFormat EnglishLanguage SoftwareBug "software bug")

(forall (?BUG)
  (=> (instance ?BUG SoftwareBug)
      (exists (?PROG)
        (and (instance ?PROG ComputerProgram)
             (part ?BUG ?PROG)
             (not (equal ?BUG ?PROG))))))

(forall (?BUG ?PROG ?PROC)
  (=> (and (instance ?BUG SoftwareBug)
           (instance ?PROG ComputerProgram)
           (part ?BUG ?PROG)
           (instance ?PROC ComputerProcess)
           (realization ?PROC ?PROG)
           (causes ?BUG ?PROC))
      (exists (?PURPOSE)
        (and (hasPurpose ?PROG ?PURPOSE)
             (not (realization ?PROC ?PURPOSE))))))